      "summary": "The heredoc marker check addresses the prior heredoc bypass, but the replacement boundary introduces a reachable truncation path for locals containing a column-zero nested-object brace.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/release-identity.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 423,
          "message": "The new block boundary can truncate a locals scan at a column-zero nested-object brace, allowing a later credential-bearing local referenced by an output to evade AC RELEASE-ID-04.",
          "confidence": 0.88,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The changed block scan ends at the first line matching ^}. It rejects blocks containing a heredoc marker, but a multiline object inside locals can also close at column zero and truncate the scan before later local assignments.",
            "failureScenario": "If a locals block contains a multiline object whose closing brace starts at column zero, followed by hidden_key = azurerm_storage_account.demo.primary_access_key, the scan stops before hidden_key. An output referencing local.hidden_key contains no credential attribute in its source, and the evaluated opaque key may match none of the text patterns. The test can pass while an output exposes storage-key material, contrary to AC RELEASE-ID-04."
          }
        }
      ]
